---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SocialIcon from '../components/SocialIcon.astro';
import { SITE, SOCIALS } from '../data/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`About — ${SITE.name}`}
  description={`Who ${SITE.name} is, what the blog covers, and where to find him.`}
>
  <div class="wrap wrap-narrow">
    <header class="page-head">
      <p class="kicker">About</p>
      <h1>Hey — I'm Brendan.</h1>
      <p class="post-lede">
        I build PCs, take hardware apart, and write down what actually happened. This blog is where
        the long version of my videos and posts lives.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose page-body">
      <p>
        Most of what I make starts the same way: a part arrives, I have a theory about how it will
        behave, and the theory turns out to be half right. The videos show the build. The posts here
        are for the parts that need numbers, screenshots, or a paragraph of context — thermals that
        did not match the review sites, a BIOS setting that quietly cost 8% of a benchmark, a cable
        run I would do differently next time.
      </p>

      <h2>What I write about</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Builds</strong> — full part lists, what they cost, and what I would change.</li>
        <li>
          <strong>Hardware</strong> — cooling, cases, PSUs, and the specs that actually matter.
        </li>
        <li><strong>Homelab</strong> — the machines that run in the closet and stay on.</li>
        <li><strong>Benchmarks</strong> — how I test, and where the numbers came from.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How I test</h2>
      <p>
        Every benchmark post lists the full bench, the driver versions, ambient temperature, and how
        many runs went into the number. If I cannot reproduce a result twice, it does not get
        published. When I get something wrong, I update the post and note what changed at the top
        rather than quietly editing it.
      </p>

      <h2>Get in touch</h2>
      <p>
        The fastest way to reach me is a reply on any of the accounts below — I am
        <strong>{SITE.handle}</strong> on all of them. For anything longer,
        <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>email works too</a>.
      </p>
    </div>

    <section class="page-body" aria-labelledby="find-me">
      <h2 id="find-me" class="visually-hidden">Find me</h2>
      <ul class="socials">
        {
          SOCIALS.map((social) => (
            <li>
              <a class="social-link" href={social.href} rel="me noopener" target="_blank">
                <SocialIcon name={social.icon} />
                {social.label}
              </a>
            </li>
          ))
        }
        <li>
          <a class="social-link" href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>
            <SocialIcon name="email" />
            Email
          </a>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
